# What `nix build` leaves behind - a symlink into the store, not a
# source, and one that has been committed by mistake before. No
# trailing slash: it is a symlink, and `result/` would match only a
# directory. `result-*` for the numbered ones a second build makes.
result
result-*

# What the spago wrapper drops on its way past. A build timing and a
# spec run are not sources, and a night that commits one has proposed
# a change that fixes nothing. `.tmp*` rather than the one name it
# writes today, and no trailing slash, so the next thing it drops is
# covered whether it turns out to be a directory or a file.
.tmp*
